## lem-ask

`skills/lem-ask/` is adapted from the `huddle` plugin in
[skkap/claude-skills](https://github.com/skkap/claude-skills), as of commit
`29d6db7` (huddle 1.0.0).

Retained as published: the JSON spec and its answer contract, the `q`
one-liner, the runtime (`huddle.js`, `huddle.css`) with its blocks, charts,
mermaid diagrams, controls with live preview, multi-question tabs and review
screen, the four styles, the keyboard map, the agterm overlay open-and-poll
loop with `huddle wait` resume, the sidebar status glyph, the browser
fallback, `~/.config/huddle/defaults.json`, and the ten templates and five
demos.

Changes made: the skill, its command and its runtime files have new names (`lem-ask`,
`bin/lem-ask`, `ask.js`, `ask.css`), and its personal defaults moved to
the table `[ask]` of Lem's own `~/.config/lem/settings.toml`, and its mermaid cache to `~/.cache/lem/`; the launcher moved from the skill's
`scripts/huddle.py` to `bin/lem-ask`, so it is a bare command on the Bash tool's `PATH` and
`allowed-tools: Bash(lem-ask *)` pre-authorizes it; it refuses to open a page
in an unattended run (`CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ATTENDED=0`); outside agterm the
browser fallback is opt-in (`--browser` or `browser = true` in the user's
defaults) instead of automatic, and `HUDDLE_NO_BROWSER` is gone; an occupied overlay
slot is its own exit (5, `busy`), naming the page when it is a question page; `lem-ask wait` fails at once on an agterm
error instead of reporting `pending` after the full timeout; a malformed spec
gets the JSON error contract instead of a traceback; the downloaded mermaid
bundle is checked against a pinned sha256; `code`, `diff`, `md` and `mermaid`
blocks can read their text from a file, with line numbers for code and a
300-line cap on a whole file; a `q`
option takes a third `|why` field; `api.select` on a single-choice question
replaces the selection instead of adding to it; a Stop hook re-posts the asking
glyph when a turn ends with a question page still open, and a timed-out question
posts its glyph with `--auto-reset`; a question's `context` renders like its `body`, keys the page does not read
are rejected, and options labeled only by position are refused; the skill's description and
"when to ask" rules were rewritten to defer to the user's own instructions and
to keep subagents and unattended runs from asking; spelling is American.

